- Customized Windows settings
- Monitored CPU, Memory, and Disk usage
- Explored Windows Security features
- Performed a custom antivirus scan
- Reviewed Firewall settings

---

## 🔑 Key Takeaways

- Windows uses a Graphical User Interface (GUI) to simplify system interaction.
- File Explorer is the primary tool for navigating and managing files.
- Task Manager provides real-time performance monitoring.
- Windows Security helps protect the system against malware and threats.
- Windows Defender Firewall filters incoming and outgoing network traffic.
- Understanding the Windows interface is essential before learning advanced Windows administration and cybersecurity concepts.

